{"id": "EUVD-2026-82126", "enisaUuid": "65c84f9a-957d-3a51-ae09-c1b8e840c632", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niommu/amd: Fix undefined behavior in devid_write debugfs function\n\nWhen for_each_pci_segment() loop completes without finding a matching\nsegment, the pci_seg pointer is not NULL but points to an invalid memory\nlocation (the list head). Accessing pci_seg->id after the loop causes\nundefined behavior.\n\nFix this by handling the successful case inside the loop and returning\n-EINVAL after the loop if no matching segment is found.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:04:11", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8aabe0fba01486b5d893e708b05a8fa7f1b7efbb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/99d42aef089a07cfb1d404a7227ac9dc7628b497", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/843e149989665f8309ad2efe6048dc76591e1f94"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-92505", "GHSA-2mxc-qwhf-8gfr"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0837ac1c-ed24-32e8-8267-23d86e5d85aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2e98940f123d9c69d4759078aea9a536244c98d3 <843e149989665f8309ad2efe6048dc76591e1f94"}, {"id": "2dcd45cc-56c0-3414-bdc2-8f58c763f146", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2e98940f123d9c69d4759078aea9a536244c98d3 <8aabe0fba01486b5d893e708b05a8fa7f1b7efbb"}, {"id": "320bce94-1e35-348d-adba-06b15e317a85", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3e184ae4-88ac-3658-8fa6-abbc1c85212f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2e98940f123d9c69d4759078aea9a536244c98d3 <99d42aef089a07cfb1d404a7227ac9dc7628b497"}, {"id": "44108ca1-7710-3e24-b10d-4e8a73476969", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "5ef1cb84-6aa2-32ce-9cb